        "locked": false,
        "title": "[Enhancement] Support dynamic batching and deferred queue writes for audit log persistence",
        "body": "The audit log event store performs synchronous SQLite database transactions immediately upon recording any audit event (starts, completions, tool calls). Under high concurrency or during extensive tool execution cycles, this causes transaction contention, database locking, and blocks active execution.\n\nProposed Solution:\nIntroduce a deferred write queue that batches audit events and flushes them to SQLite asynchronously, separating logging transactions from execution hot paths.\n\nSource Reference:\nsrc/audit/audit-event-store.ts#L578-L600",
